        "body": "The hub now uses the `openbao_backup` role from #215, so OpenBao's snapshot is backed up nightly into the hub's own repository and copied to B2 like the other three machines (Backups decisions 72 and 74, Platform decision 9).\n\n**What changes.**\n- `host_vars/hub.yml` makes the hub a machine: a `hub` entry in `b2_buckets` (`keepbreathing-hub-backup`), a `hub` login in `backup_server_logins`, a `hub` entry in `b2_copy_passwords`, and the four `openbao_backup_*` variables, all from the vault item `rclone hub (hub)`.\n- The `openbao-snapshot` AppRole now belongs to the backup account, so the next real `openbao_config` run moves its files there.\n- `playbooks/hub.yml` runs `openbao_backup` as the last task of its services play, after `svc:openbao` is served, tagged `openbao_backup`. A rebuilt hub's first run can skip it with `--skip-tags openbao_backup`, so it never backs up an empty OpenBao.\n\n**Tests.** A new `test_hub_openbao_backup.py` pins the hub's new inventory entries. `test_hub_services_order.py` now also checks that the role's tasks come last, and that `--skip-tags openbao_backup` removes all of them while keeping the rest in order. The vault render test covers the hub's login and the role's two passwords. Because `host_vars/hub.yml` changes, CI runs every driver job.\n\n**Before the first live run** the vault needs the item `rclone hub (hub)`, shaped like the other machines' items.\n\nCloses #220\n",
