      "body": "### Project, step, and reason\n\nOpenBao on the hub, Next 4.3b. pfnet's alertmanager-to-github turns alerts into issues in platform-tickets, signing in as the keepbreath-ticket-band GitHub App with a key from OpenBao. It has no authentication, so nginx in the same pod is the only way in: posts need Alertmanager's password, and nginx replaces the query string so no post can choose labels.\n\nDesign: ~/Documents/Second_Brain/10_Projects/14_Security/OpenBao on the hub.md, decisions 12, 17, 20, 23, 30, 36, 43, 50, 72 and 76.\n\n### What changes\n\n- ticket_band's main tasks add a Quadlet pod in the band's account with pfnet and nginx, pfnet taking the App key as a Podman secret holding ticket-band/app-key, and the pod waiting on the boot cleanup with Wants= and After=.\n- nginx takes POST /v1/webhook only with Alertmanager's password and replaces the query with a rewrite, lets GET /metrics through, and refuses everything else.\n- The hub role adds the ticket receiver to Alertmanager's config with basic_auth and a password file, and gives Alertmanager's container the loopback network line Prometheus has. No route sends to the receiver yet.\n\n### Done when\n\nThe ticket-band driver shows the gate's answers through the pod, the boot cleanup finishing before the pod starts, and with the cleanup made to hang the pod starting once it is killed and the receiver answering; the full check passes on the same commit; and the build has passed Claude's review.\n",
